# What the deployed site does NOT carry.
#
# The Beluga runtime is served from R2 (beljar-cdn.deanbarry.com), uploaded with
# each rebuild (_rebuild/RECIPE.md, Deploying): it was once over Cloudflare's
# 25 MiB per-file static-asset cap, and it changes far less often than the site.
# edit.html points at the bucket on deployed hosts; locally it loads from this repo.
# The JS build (the fallback where Wasm cannot run):
beluga_web.bc.js
# The two wasm_of_ocaml builds (the default, beluga_web_wasm_cps): each a loader
# plus a folder of content-hashed .wasm.
beluga_web_wasm*.bc.wasm.js
beluga_web_wasm*.bc.wasm.assets

# The repository itself. wrangler skips nothing on its own (only .assetsignore,
# _redirects and _headers), and the Git build deploys from a clone, so until
# 2026-09-28 the live site served /.git/ (config, index, every object).
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.gitmodules
.nojekyll

# Source, tooling and docs — none of it is fetched at runtime.
node_modules
# the sync Worker's source and its local config: code the Worker runs, never a file it serves
server
.wrangler
wrangler.jsonc
Beluga-W
_rebuild
tests
scripts
scratch
# the kit page: every component on one page, for looking at (dev/kit.html)
dev
results
docs
.cursor
.idea
.claude
*.md
beluga.grammar
eslint.config.mjs
package.json
package-lock.json
